Subject: [PATCH] mailbox: qcom-ipcc: reserve channels for SM-X910 runtime DSPs

The SM-X910 port creates some DSP endpoints after IPCC has probed, because
changing the boot DTB layout breaks Samsung ABL. Counting only clients
present at probe reserves seven channels; ADSP, CDSP, SPSS and MPSS need
eight when combined with SMP2P and AOSS. MPSS plus CDSP then fails with
-EBUSY even though the requested client/signal pair is unused.

On this board reserve at least the 48 channels used by Samsung's downstream
IPCC driver. This changes allocation capacity only, not interrupt routing.

--- a/drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c
+++ b/drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c
@@ -234,6 +234,10 @@ static int qcom_ipcc_setup_mbox(struct qcom_ipcc *ipcc,
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* Late-created SM-X910 DSP endpoints are absent from the initial DT. */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("samsung,gts9uwifi"))
+		ipcc->num_chans = max(ipcc->num_chans, 48);
+
 	/* If no clients are found, skip registering as a mbox controller */
 	if (!ipcc->num_chans)
 		return 0;
